    <node id="吴国">
      <data key="d0">吴国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 吴国 refers to an important state during the Spring and Autumn period in ancient China, known for its significant political and military power. It was ruled by King Fucha and stood as a major rival and enemy to the neighboring state of 越国 (Yue). 吴国 was involved in intense conflicts and territorial struggles, notably against 越国 and other prominent states such as 齐国 (Qi) and 晋国 (Jin), positioning itself as a key player in the regional rivalry among these powerful states.

吴国 held a reputation for exceptional craftsmanship, especially in sword-making. This excellence is associated with legendary swordsmiths such as the couple 干将 and 莫邪, as well as the renowned swordsmith 风师哥, whose works were highly prized. The country is also connected to notable historical figures like 伍子胥, a loyal minister and military strategist, who contributed to 吴国’s military strength and strategic endeavors.

The capital of 吴国 was the royal palace of King Fucha, which symbolized the state's central authority and cultural significance. Despite its initial dominance and flourishing power, 吴国 ultimately suffered military defeat when 越国 launched successful campaigns that led to the downfall of 吴国’s control. The history of 吴国 is therefore marked by both its cultural achievements and its dramatic military confrontations during the Spring and Autumn period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71</data>
